olr controls a Linux box running open-linux-router.

Most commands talk to the olr service over its control socket. The ones
under Service manage that service itself, and work without it running.

Usage:
  olr [command]

Modules:
  dhcp        DHCP server (dnsmasq)
  dns         DNS resolver and policy (olr-dnsd + unbound)
  firewall    Let something on the internet reach one device here
  gateway     Exits and which networks use them
  link        Network interfaces olr has been given

Operations:
  adopt       Take ownership of an interface
  diff        Show drifted or pending configuration, per module
  history     List configuration revisions, per module
  release     Hand an interface back to the system
  rollback    Roll a module back to an earlier revision
  status      Report whether olr is running

Service:
  disable     Stop olr, and stop it starting at boot
  enable      Run olr on this box, now and after every reboot
  listen      Serve the web UI on a network address
  restart     Restart olr
  start       Start olr
  stop        Stop olr

Other:
  completion  Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell
  help        Help about any command
  version     Print version information

Flags:
      --dry-run         show what would change and exit without applying it
  -h, --help            help for olr
  -o, --output string   output format: text|json (default "text")
      --socket string   olrd control socket (default "/run/olr/olrd.sock")

Use "olr [command] --help" for more information about a command.
